✔ Story & World hosts the writing workspace and keeps one primary action and the format foot; the build questions wait in a dialog (10.9122ms)
✔ the build dialog asks how to split, the ratio and the style, has one primary action and a way to import a shot table (11.6913ms)
✔ the dialog shows what each way of splitting would give, marks the one nearest the target, and fails soft (14.0225ms)
✔ the space menu lists what each space needs as items of their own, never a button inside a button (6.1044ms)
✔ adapting preserves the original source and screenplay edits while a changed source requires a fresh adaptation (1.3967ms)
✔ a composition carries lenses and the choice trace; no lens is the classic request (0.3045ms)
✔ a composed adaptation sends lenses and the trace, returns the no-label report, and a changed choice needs a fresh adaptation (1.0268ms)
